[
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/analytics.ts",
    "line": 6,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`trackAppEvent` now calls `track()` without guarding against runtime exceptions. Previously analytics failures were explicitly swallowed so they could not interrupt the search flow; consider restoring a try/catch (or a safe no-op fallback) so a tracking failure can’t break user interactions.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:53Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/page.tsx",
    "line": 140,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "The clipboard write failure path rethrows any non-`DOMException` error. If `navigator.clipboard.writeText()` rejects with a plain `Error` (which can happen outside spec-ideal environments), this will surface as an unhandled exception and skip the intended user-facing status message. Consider treating clipboard failures as non-fatal (don’t rethrow) or broadening the recoverable check.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:53Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/browserErrors.ts",
    "line": 17,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`isRecoverableStorageWriteError` only treats `DOMException` as recoverable (same pattern for clipboard). Callers rethrow when this returns false, so a storage/clipboard implementation that rejects with a plain `Error` will crash the UI for an optional feature. Consider broadening these guards (e.g., accept `Error` and check `name`) or making callers always swallow these failures.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 31,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`getStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows for any storage read error that isn’t a `DOMException`/`SyntaxError`. Since this function is called during page load and recent searches are a convenience feature, rethrowing can break the homepage unexpectedly. Consider returning an empty list for any error instead of throwing.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 49,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`saveStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows non-`DOMException` errors from `localStorage.setItem`. Recent search persistence is non-critical; rethrowing here can break an otherwise successful search flow. Consider swallowing all storage write errors (or broadening the recoverable classification) so searches still succeed.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 62,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`clearStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows non-`DOMException` errors from `localStorage.removeItem`. Clearing recent searches should be best-effort; rethrowing risks turning an optional cleanup into a user-visible crash. Consider swallowing all errors here.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  }
]
