    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 31,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`getStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows for any storage read error that isn’t a `DOMException`/`SyntaxError`. Since this function is called during page load and recent searches are a convenience feature, rethrowing can break the homepage unexpectedly. Consider returning an empty list for any error instead of throwing.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 49,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`saveStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows non-`DOMException` errors from `localStorage.setItem`. Recent search persistence is non-critical; rethrowing here can break an otherwise successful search flow. Consider swallowing all storage write errors (or broadening the recoverable classification) so searches still succeed.",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  },
  {
    "author": "Copilot",
    "path": "app/home/recentSearches.ts",
    "line": 62,
    "side": "RIGHT",
    "body": "`clearStoredRecentSearches()` rethrows non-`DOMException` errors from `localStorage.removeItem`. Clearing recent searches should be best-effort; rethrowing risks turning an optional cleanup into a user-visible crash. Consider swallowing all errors here.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-05-25T05:49:54Z"
  }
]
